{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792335419,"nonce":"gqJIt9kfSHqqsI0ahbqg69/RPDE=","title":"Reopening a Floating panel while it is closing, then closing it, aborts the process","message":"**What happens**\nA Floating (modeless) panel is opened, closed, and opened again while its closing animation is still playing; closing it a second time aborts the process with a taffy panic, `invalid SlotMap key used` (tree/taffy_tree.rs:621). It is a native panic, not a Haxe exception, so it takes the app down.\n\n**Reproducer** (offscreen, from RayDE's command center)\nOpen it; set `open` false; advance about 3 frames of 1/60 s; set `open` true; advance 30 frames; set `open` false; advance 40 frames. The abort is inside Offscreen.advance, from Element.remove in a callback, probably `Animations.whenPlayed`'s finish. Opening in the same frame as the close, or after the animation has played, is fine. A person can hit it with Escape then Cmd+P quickly.\n\n**What reading it suggests**\nTopEntry.close calls onClose at once, so Floating's `entry` is null, and removes the layer only when Animations.whenPlayed fires. A reopen in between makes a second entry and moves the panel into a new layer; the first entry's finish then runs and removes a node that is no longer where it was, or twice.\n\n**Wanted**\nNo abort. A snapshot test of its own with the reproducer above.\n\n**Reported by** chimpmonk-af (RayDE bug f775096, worked around in RayDE by holding the reopen back until the animation has played, commit 205edc7).","files":null}]}